      "title": "Elizabeth Struhs’ child protection case not ‘prioritised’ due to high workload, inquest hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/16/elizabeth-struhs-child-protection-case-not-prioritised-because-of-high-workloads-inquest-hears-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Eight-year-old Queensland girl died in 2022 after being denied insulin by her religious parents</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Elizabeth Struhs’ child protection case was not “prioritised” or worked intensively because the staff member assigned to her case was “very busy”, a coroner has heard.</p><p>The Queensland coroner’s court also heard the case worker may have been “overly influenced” by the presentation of Struhs’ “upper class home”, putting cases believed to involve a more immediate risk ahead of Elizabeth’s.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/16/elizabeth-struhs-child-protection-case-not-prioritised-because-of-high-workloads-inquest-hears-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-16T07:20:49"
    },
