      "title": "One Nation proposes $2,000 baby subsidy in Victoria but says it won’t touch state abortion laws",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/16/one-nation-birth-subsidy-victoria-abortion-laws-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Announcement comes a day after Liberal and Labor parties say they will cover out-of-pocket costs for abortion care</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>One Nation has proposed a $2,000 baby bonus for new parents in Victoria – a day after the Labor and Liberal parties both agreed to cover out-of-pocket costs for abortion care.</p><p>The deputy leader of One Nation in Victoria, Colleen Harkin, announced the plan on Friday to remove out-of-pocket costs for pregnant women in the public healthcare system and a $2,000 subsidy for those accessing private maternity care.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/16/one-nation-birth-subsidy-victoria-abortion-laws-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-16T07:03:45"
    },
    {
      "title": "Exclusive Brethren head denies knowing church members were volunteering for Liberal party during 2025 election",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/16/exclusive-brethren-head-denies-knowing-church-members-volunteering-liberal-party-2025-election-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Bruce Hales also denies church was a cult while son tells parliamentary committee it was ‘a bit rough’ being labelled as such</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The most senior member of the Exclusive Brethren has denied any knowledge of or involvement in thousands of members from his church volunteering for the Liberal party at the 2025 election.</p><p>The Plymouth Brethren christian church has rejected claims it coordinated volunteers and a campaign for the Coalition, and that it secretly paid far-right figures to stage stunts against the prime minister and other Labor MPs.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/16/exclusive-brethren-head-denies-knowing-church-members-volunteering-liberal-party-2025-election-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
